// Achievements window.
//
// Same visual language as game_bao and game_bazaar -- layered dark surfaces,
// the client's own 3-state button artwork, and one documented colour scale.
// A player who has learned to read one of those three windows can read this
// one without being taught anything new.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Design tokens (shared with bazaar.otui / bao.otui).
//
//   SURFACES   #262626  card cap / list ground (deepest)
//              #2b2b2b  card ground, UNEARNED
//              #333333  card ground, earned
//              #3a3a3a  raised band (card footer, filter bar, header)
//              #4a4a4a  hairline / divider
//              #6a6a6a  border on interactive elements
//
//   TEXT       #f6f1e2  primary   (earned achievement names)
//              #c8c8c8  secondary (labels, controls)
//              #9a9a9a  tertiary  (meta, counts, rarity)
//              #7a7a7a  unearned name
//              #5f5f5f  unearned body text
//
//   ACCENT     #f0c674  points gold -- used ONLY for an achievement-point value
//              #8fd97f  earned green -- used ONLY to say "you have this"
//              #e8825c  ember -- used ONLY for "nobody on this server has
//                       earned this yet", the single most interesting fact
//                       this window can tell a player
//
//   DIFFICULTY #3f6b3a  Easy      (dim #2c4a29)
//              #2f5a7d  Medium    (dim #223f57)
//              #7a2c2c  Hard      (dim #4f1d1d)
//
// Difficulty is the one place a fourth hue enters, and it is carried on a 3px
// rail and a chip -- never on text. That keeps it readable as a category
// rather than competing with the three accents, which all mean something.
//
// Spacing is a 4px rhythm: 4 / 6 / 10 / 16.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Surfaces. Not colours -- the CLIENT's own assets, the same three every other
// window in this codebase is built from (see docs/client-ui-guide.md). What
// was here before was a palette of flat fills inside 1px borders, which is a
// wireframe: Tibia's interface has no flat rectangles in it anywhere, so a
// window made of them reads as a web page rendered inside a game.
//
// The one deliberate exception is HsPlaque / HsFace further down. That is the
// showcase plaque, and it is meant to be the single thing on the page wearing
// a material nothing else has.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// (!) THE DEPTH STACK. Measured, not chosen by eye. image-color MULTIPLIES the
// asset, so the number in a style is not the colour you get -- what you get is
// (asset centre x tint). Outermost to innermost:
//
//   #444444  the client's own window ground (/images/ui/window), the datum
//   #2c2c2c  list container   panel_flat x #a4a4a4   sunken
//   #414141  card / panel     2px-light  x #f0f0f0   raised
//   #353535  well inside it   panel_flat x #c4c4c4   sunken
//   #1a1a1a  slot / groove    item.png   x #b4b4b4   items and meters ONLY
//
// This replaced a stack of #2a card / #17 well built on the DARK 2-pixel frame
// and on item.png -- the inventory weave, the darkest surface the client
// ships. Individually each looked deliberate; together they made a window
// three steps darker than the game around it. item.png is right behind an ITEM
// and behind a progress groove, and wrong everywhere else.

// RAISED. The client's 2-pixel up-frame in its LIGHT weight.
AchPlate < Panel
  image-source: /images/ui/2pixel-up-frame-borderimage
  image-border: 2
  image-color: #f0f0f0

// SUNKEN, GREY. corelib's FlatPanel asset. A card's cap band sits IN it.
AchWell < Panel
  image-source: /images/ui/panel_flat
  image-border: 1
  image-color: #c4c4c4

// A GROOVE. A ProgressBar paints its background-color AS THE FILL, so the
// track under it has to be genuinely dark for the fill to read.
AchGroove < Panel
  image-source: /images/ui/item
  image-border: 1
  image-color: #9c9c9c

// A rule -- the client's own separator artwork, a dark groove over a light
// highlight, so it reads as engraved into the surface rather than drawn on
// top of it. Same asset corelib's HorizontalSeparator uses.
AchSep < UIWidget
  height: 2
  image-source: /images/ui/separator_horizontal
  image-border: 1
  phantom: true
  focusable: false

// (!) No fill. This was a filled pill, and with the grade, Secret and
// Showcased all wearing one, a single card could carry six coloured objects --
// three pills, gold points, a green earned-date and an amber rarity line --
// before the rail. Fifteen of those on screen is a colour field, not a list.
//
// Tibia states things with COLOURED TEXT on grey, and it spends colour once.
// The chip is now a word: the grade keeps its colour, everything else is grey,
// and the rail down the card's left edge carries the same grade colour so the
// grid is still scannable by difficulty at arm's length.
AchChip < Label
  height: 14
  font: verdana-11px-monochrome
  color: #c8c8c8
  text-align: left
  phantom: true

// ProgressBar paints its own background-color AS THE FILL, scaled by percent --
// there is no separate track colour -- so the dark groove behind one has to
// come from the panel it sits on.
AchMeter < ProgressBar
  height: 5
  background-color: #f0c674

AchPointsBar < ProgressBar
  height: 16
  background-color: #6f9e58
  font: verdana-11px-monochrome

// (!) /images/ui/buttons, not button_rounded, and no brass tint. Same change
// and same reasoning as game_store's StoreButton -- these windows share one
// chrome and these styles are copies of each other. This was the last
// button_rounded left in the codebase.
//
// button_rounded is a smooth grey gradient: the one control in the window made
// of no material while every panel around it is textured slate. The brass tint
// also put window chrome in the same colour as the showcase plaque, so a
// utility wore the accent that is supposed to mean "this is the showcased
// one".
//
// /images/ui/buttons is what data/styles/10-buttons.otui puts on every button
// in this client: 43x40 as two states of 20 -- normal at y=0, pressed at y=20
// -- 9-sliced at image-border 3 so the noise tiles at any width. The native
// style reuses the normal clip for $hover because real Tibia buttons do not
// light up; this one does, through image-color, which is why rest is #d8d8d8
// rather than full brightness (image-color MULTIPLIES).
AchButton < UIButton
  height: 21
  font: verdana-11px-monochrome
  image-source: /images/ui/buttons
  image-clip: 0 0 43 20
  image-border: 3
  image-color: #d8d8d8
  color: #e8e8e8
  text-offset: 0 1
  change-cursor-image: true
  cursor: pointer

  $hover !disabled:
    image-color: #ffffff
    color: #ffffff

  $pressed:
    image-clip: 0 20 43 20
    text-offset: 1 2

  $disabled:
    image-color: #7d7d7d
    color: #9a9a9a
    change-cursor-image: false

// A read-out plate in the header. Solid, not phantom: Panel is phantom:true by
// default, so the plate would never receive the mouse and its tooltip could
// never fire -- and every figure in this header needs to explain itself.
AchBalance < FlatPanel
  image-color: #9a9a9a
  height: 21
  focusable: false
  phantom: false

  Label
    id: value
    anchors.fill: parent
    margin-left: 8
    margin-right: 8
    text-align: right
    text: 0
    font: verdana-11px-rounded
    color: #f6f1e2

  Label
    id: caption
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
    margin-left: 8
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #9a9a9a
    phantom: true

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Difficulty read-out.
//
// Three of these across the bottom of the header answer "how am I doing" for
// the whole catalogue without scrolling a single card -- which is the entire
// reason the header is two rows tall instead of one.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AchGradeMeter < Panel
  height: 28
  phantom: true

  Label
    id: caption
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.left: parent.left
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #c8c8c8
    text-auto-resize: true

  Label
    id: count
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.right: parent.right
    text-align: right
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #9a9a9a
    text-auto-resize: true

  // The groove a meter runs in. ProgressBar paints its background-color AS
  // THE FILL, so the track behind it has to be a real surface underneath.
  AchGroove
    id: track
    height: 5
    anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    margin-bottom: 4

    AchMeter
      id: bar
      anchors.fill: parent

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The card.
//
// Reads in one glance, top to bottom: what kind of thing this is (rail and
// chip), what it is worth (gold, right of the cap), what it is (name), what it
// asks of you (description), how rare it is and whether you have it (footer).
//
// An unearned card is the same card dimmed, never a different card. Players
// scan a grid by shape; changing the shape for locked entries would make the
// grid unreadable at the exact density this window is built for.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AchCard < AchPlate
  size: 288 122
  focusable: false
  phantom: false
  // Base state is UNEARNED: the same frame, dimmed. See the note in
  // achievements.lua's fillCard for why earned and showcased are widget STATES
  // here rather than colours set from Lua.
  image-color: #b0b0b0

  // Earned.
  $on:
    image-color: #f0f0f0

  // Showcased -- brighter still, warmed toward the plaque. Declared after $on
  // because a showcased card is also earned and both blocks match; the later
  // one wins for the tags they share.
  $checked:
    image-color: #ffe8b8

  // Declared last so hovering wins over both. image-color MULTIPLIES, which is
  // why no resting state sits at full brightness.
  $hover:
    image-color: #ffffff

  Panel
    id: rail
    width: 3
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    background-color: #3f6b3a
    phantom: true

  AchWell
    id: cap
    height: 20
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.left: rail.right
    anchors.right: parent.right
    phantom: true

    AchChip
      id: grade
      anchors.left: parent.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 7

    AchChip
      id: secret
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 8
      color: #9a9a9a
      text: Secret
      visible: false

    Label
      id: points
      anchors.right: parent.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 9
      font: verdana-11px-rounded
      color: #f0c674
      text-auto-resize: true

    // (!) Anchored to `points`, not to the chips on the left. `secret` is
    // hidden on most cards, and a hidden widget keeps its rect -- anchoring a
    // chain to it would leave a gap on every non-secret card.
    AchChip
      id: showcase
      anchors.right: points.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 8
      text-align: right
      color: #c8c8c8
      text: Showcased
      visible: false

  Label
    id: name
    height: 15
    anchors.top: cap.bottom
    anchors.left: rail.right
    anchors.right: parent.right
    margin-top: 6
    margin-left: 10
    margin-right: 10
    font: verdana-11px-rounded
    color: #f6f1e2

  // (!) Anchored top AND bottom rather than given a height. The descriptions
  // range from one line to five; a fixed height would either clip the long
  // ones or leave a hole under the short ones.
  Label
    id: description
    anchors.top: name.bottom
    anchors.left: rail.right
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.bottom: footRule.top
    margin-top: 3
    margin-left: 10
    margin-right: 10
    margin-bottom: 4
    text-wrap: true
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #8f8f8f

  AchSep
    id: footRule
    anchors.bottom: foot.top
    anchors.left: rail.right
    anchors.right: parent.right

  // The footer is a sunken band, the same surface as the cap above it. That
  // gives the card the shape a Tibia record has -- a header strip, a raised
  // face carrying the text, and a footer strip -- rather than one open panel
  // with lines drawn across it.
  AchWell
    id: foot
    height: 22
    anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
    anchors.left: rail.right
    anchors.right: parent.right
    phantom: true

    Label
      id: rarity
      anchors.left: parent.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 10
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #9a9a9a
      text-auto-resize: true

    Label
      id: status
      anchors.right: parent.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 10
      text-align: right
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #8fd97f
      text-auto-resize: true

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


// ---------------- highscores ----------------
//
// The blend the brief asked for: the CLIENT keeps its dark stone panels and
// its own button sprite, and what comes across from the website is the gold
// bevel around a recessed face and the lit-gold numeral inside it. That is the
// same plaque the character page's Achievement showcase wears, translated to a
// dark surface -- a cream face that works on parchment would be a hole punched
// in this window.

HsPlaque < Panel
  background-color: #a8925e
  padding: 2

HsFace < Panel
  background-color: #2f2a1d
  border-width: 1
  border-color: #6b5a34

// A board key. AchButton carries the hover, pressed and disabled states and the
// gold image tint, so a board button is that button at list scale -- plus the
// one state it does NOT define. AchButton has no $checked, so setChecked() on
// a plain AchButton changes nothing at all and the open board would look
// identical to the eleven you are not on. This adds it, reusing the pressed
// sprite and its 1px text drop so "current" reads as held down.
HsBoardButton < AchButton
  height: 20
  margin-right: 4

  // The gold stays HERE and nowhere else on a button: "this is the board you
  // are looking at" is the one button state in this window worth an accent.
  $checked:
    image-clip: 0 20 43 20
    image-color: #f0c674
    color: #ffffff
    text-offset: 1 2

// One ranked line. Built in Lua by the dozen, so every column is a fixed
// anchor rather than a layout -- a grid layout here would relayout the whole
// list on each fill.
HsRow < UIWidget
  height: 22
  focusable: false
  phantom: false

  Label
    id: rank
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
    margin-left: 8
    width: 46
    text-align: right
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #9a9a9a

  Label
    id: value
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
    margin-right: 10
    width: 120
    text-align: right
    font: verdana-11px-antialised
    color: #f0c674

  Label
    id: extra
    anchors.right: value.left
    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
    margin-right: 16
    width: 150
    text-align: right
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #9a9a9a

  Label
    id: name
    anchors.left: rank.right
    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
    margin-left: 14
    width: 220
    font: verdana-11px-antialised
    color: #dfdfdf

  Label
    id: vocation
    anchors.left: name.right
    anchors.right: extra.left
    anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
    margin-left: 8
    margin-right: 8
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #7f7f7f

HsTabPanel < Panel

  // Board keys on the left, the two choosers on the right -- the same
  // arrangement the website settled on, so a player who knows one knows the
  // other.
  AchPlate
    id: boardBar
    height: 31
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right

    ComboBox
      id: vocationFilter
      anchors.right: parent.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 10
      width: 132

    ComboBox
      id: skillFilter
      anchors.right: prev.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 6
      width: 132

    Panel
      id: boardButtons
      anchors.left: parent.left
      anchors.right: skillFilter.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      height: 20
      margin-left: 8
      margin-right: 10
      layout:
        type: horizontalBox

  // The leader. Hidden entirely when the top score is zero or tied -- see the
  // note in achievements_protocol.lua for why crowning an arbitrary one of
  // five characters on zero is worse than crowning nobody.
  HsPlaque
    id: champPlate
    height: 96
    anchors.top: boardBar.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    margin-top: 8

    HsFace
      id: champFace
      anchors.fill: parent

      // The window's real advantage over the website: this is the live outfit,
      // drawn by the client, not a 64x64 GIF fetched from an image service.
      Creature
        id: champCreature
        size: 72 72
        anchors.left: parent.left
        anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
        margin-left: 10

      Label
        id: champEyebrow
        anchors.top: parent.top
        anchors.left: champCreature.right
        margin-top: 14
        margin-left: 14
        font: verdana-11px-monochrome
        color: #8a7a55
        text-auto-resize: true
        text: RANK 1

      // (!) Verdana Bold-16px. data/fonts declares exactly one large Verdana,
      // and naming a face that does not exist does not error -- it silently
      // falls back to the 11px default, which is what once made a "big" number
      // render at body size with its caption sitting at the wrong height.
      Label
        id: champName
        anchors.top: prev.bottom
        anchors.left: prev.left
        margin-top: 2
        font: Verdana Bold-16px
        color: #f0c674
        text-auto-resize: true

      Label
        id: champSub
        anchors.top: prev.bottom
        anchors.left: prev.left
        margin-top: 3
        font: verdana-11px-monochrome
        color: #9a9a9a
        text-auto-resize: true

      Label
        id: champValue
        anchors.top: parent.top
        anchors.right: parent.right
        margin-top: 18
        margin-right: 16
        font: Verdana Bold-16px
        color: #f0c674
        text-align: right
        text-auto-resize: true

      Label
        id: champUnit
        anchors.top: prev.bottom
        anchors.right: prev.right
        margin-top: 2
        font: verdana-11px-monochrome
        color: #8a7a55
        text-align: right
        text-auto-resize: true

  // Column headings, so the number on the right is never unlabelled.
  AchPlate
    id: hsHead
    height: 20
    anchors.top: champPlate.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    margin-top: 8

    Label
      id: headRank
      anchors.left: parent.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 8
      width: 46
      text-align: right
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #f6f1e2
      text: Rank

    Label
      id: headValue
      anchors.right: parent.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 10
      width: 120
      text-align: right
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #f6f1e2

    Label
      id: headExtra
      anchors.right: headValue.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 16
      width: 150
      text-align: right
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #f6f1e2

    Label
      id: headName
      anchors.left: headRank.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 14
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #f6f1e2
      text: Character

  ScrollablePanel
    id: rowList
    // Sunken: a card built out of the same slate as the panel behind it has
    // only its 2px bevel to separate the two. (!) Image only, no padding --
    // the module computes this list's row geometry by hand.
    image-source: /images/ui/panel_flat
    image-border: 1
    image-color: #a4a4a4
    auto-focus: none
    anchors.top: hsHead.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.bottom: youPlate.top
    margin-top: 2
    margin-right: 14
    margin-bottom: 8
    vertical-scrollbar: rowScroll
    layout:
      type: verticalBox
      spacing: 1

  VerticalScrollBar
    id: rowScroll
    anchors.top: rowList.top
    anchors.bottom: rowList.bottom
    anchors.right: parent.right
    step: 22
    pixels-scroll: true

  Label
    id: hsNotice
    anchors.fill: rowList
    visible: false
    text-align: center
    text-wrap: true
    font: verdana-11px-rounded
    color: #9a9a9a

  // Where the viewer stands, pinned. The one thing this window can say that
  // the website cannot, because it knows who is looking.
  AchPlate
    id: youPlate
    height: 24
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.bottom: parent.bottom

    Label
      id: youText
      anchors.fill: parent
      margin-left: 10
      margin-right: 10
      text-align: left
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #9a9a9a

// The achievements tab: every widget below is exactly what used to hang off
// AchWindow directly, moved one level down so the tab bar can swap it out.
// recursiveGetChildById in achievements.lua reaches through the extra level
// unchanged, which is why the Lua needed no lookup rewrites.
AchTabPanel < Panel
  // ---------------- header ----------------
  AchPlate
    id: header
    height: 108
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right

    // (!) Verdana Bold-16px, not a 22px face. data/fonts declares exactly one
    // large Verdana -- 16px -- and naming a font that does not exist does not
    // error, it silently falls back to the default 11px face. That is what
    // made this number render at body size with the "of 1,058" beside it
    // sitting at the wrong height: the two labels were bottom-aligned for a
    // 22px box that was never 22px tall.
    Label
      id: pointsValue
      anchors.top: parent.top
      anchors.left: parent.left
      margin-top: 10
      margin-left: 16
      font: Verdana Bold-16px
      color: #f0c674
      text-auto-resize: true
      text: 0

    // Bottom-anchored, which is what puts two different type sizes on a shared
    // baseline. text-auto-resize on both sides is what makes that hold -- each
    // box is exactly its own text, so aligning the boxes aligns the text.
    Label
      id: pointsOf
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.bottom: prev.bottom
      margin-left: 6
      font: verdana-11px-rounded
      color: #9a9a9a
      text-auto-resize: true

    Label
      id: pointsCaption
      anchors.top: pointsValue.bottom
      anchors.left: pointsValue.left
      margin-top: 1
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #9a9a9a
      text-auto-resize: true
      text: Achievement Points

    AchBalance
      id: unlockedPlate
      size: 152 21
      anchors.top: parent.top
      anchors.right: parent.right
      margin-top: 11
      margin-right: 16

    AchBalance
      id: secretsPlate
      size: 152 21
      anchors.top: prev.bottom
      anchors.right: prev.right
      margin-top: 5

    // Row two. Three meters, equal thirds of the band -- the whole catalogue
    // summarised in one line of the header.
    AchGradeMeter
      id: gradeEasy
      width: 276
      anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
      anchors.left: parent.left
      margin-bottom: 8
      margin-left: 16

    AchGradeMeter
      id: gradeMedium
      width: 276
      anchors.bottom: prev.bottom
      anchors.left: prev.right
      margin-left: 16

    AchGradeMeter
      id: gradeHard
      width: 276
      anchors.bottom: prev.bottom
      anchors.left: prev.right
      margin-left: 16

  // ---------------- filter bar ----------------
  AchPlate
    id: filterBar
    height: 33
    anchors.top: header.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    margin-top: 8
    margin-right: 14

    Label
      id: searchLabel
      anchors.left: parent.left
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 12
      !text: tr('Search')
      font: verdana-11px-antialised
      color: #f6f1e2

    TextEdit
      id: searchEdit
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 8
      width: 168
      height: 20

    Label
      id: showLabel
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 16
      !text: tr('Show')
      font: verdana-11px-antialised
      color: #f6f1e2

    ComboBox
      id: showFilter
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 8
      width: 128

    Label
      id: sortLabel
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 16
      !text: tr('Sort')
      font: verdana-11px-antialised
      color: #f6f1e2

    ComboBox
      id: sortMode
      anchors.left: prev.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-left: 8
      width: 140

    Label
      id: shownCount
      anchors.right: parent.right
      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
      margin-right: 12
      text-align: right
      font: verdana-11px-monochrome
      color: #9a9a9a
      text-auto-resize: true

  // ---------------- cards ----------------
  //
  // (!) No `vertical-scrollbar` binding, on purpose -- achievements.lua drives
  // cardScroll itself.
  //
  // This panel holds a POOL of about fifteen cards, not one per achievement,
  // and the module slides them with the panel's virtual offset. Binding the
  // bar the normal way would have UIScrollArea:updateScrollBars size its range
  // from getChildrenRect, i.e. from those fifteen cards -- one screenful --
  // and the bar would report that there is nothing to scroll. The module sets
  // the range from the real row count instead. See the "Virtual list geometry"
  // note in achievements.lua for why the list is pooled at all.
  //
  // It stays a ScrollablePanel rather than a Panel for the clipping and for
  // the mouse handling; Panel is phantom, and a phantom list never sees the
  // wheel.
  ScrollablePanel
    id: cardList
    // Sunken: a card built out of the same slate as the panel behind it has
    // only its 2px bevel to separate the two. (!) Image only, no padding --
    // the module computes this list's row geometry by hand.
    image-source: /images/ui/panel_flat
    image-border: 1
    image-color: #a4a4a4
    auto-focus: none
    anchors.top: filterBar.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
    margin-top: 8
    margin-right: 14
    margin-bottom: 6
    layout:
      type: grid
      cell-size: 288 122
      cell-spacing: 6
      num-columns: 3

  // (!) Starts at an empty range rather than the UIScrollBar default of
  // -999999..999999. The module hands it a real range once it knows how many
  // rows there are; until then an empty range is what keeps the bar switched
  // off, so a wheel over the list cannot scroll a list that is not there yet.
  VerticalScrollBar
    id: cardScroll
    anchors.top: cardList.top
    anchors.bottom: cardList.bottom
    anchors.right: parent.right
    minimum: 0
    maximum: 0
    step: 32
    pixels-scroll: true

  // (!) Declared here as a SIBLING of the list, not built inside it. A widget
  // parented to a grid-layout panel is resized to the cell size, so a
  // full-width notice created in Lua would be squeezed into one 288px card
  // slot and read as a broken card rather than as a message.
  Label
    id: emptyNotice
    anchors.fill: cardList
    visible: false
    text-align: center
    text-wrap: true
    font: verdana-11px-rounded
    color: #9a9a9a


// ---------------- tabs ----------------
//
// The default TabBarButton is 18px of sprite sized to its text, which reads as
// a form control rather than as the two halves of the window. These are 34px
// with an icon, so the choice is the first thing the eye lands on.
//
// (!) UITabBar derives its children's style names from its OWN style name:
// `getStyleName() .. "Button"` and `.. "Panel"`. Renaming the bar to
// RecordsTabBar is therefore what selects RecordsTabBarButton below -- the two
// names are coupled, so neither can be renamed alone.
//
// The 9-slice (`image-border: 3`) is what lets an 18px-tall sprite stretch to
// 34 without the end caps smearing.
RecordsTabBar < TabBar
  height: 36
  Panel
    id: buttonsPanel
    anchors.fill: parent

RecordsTabBarPanel < Panel

RecordsTabBarButton < TabBarButton
  height: 34
  // (!) THE CLIP IS 96 WIDE HERE, NOT THE BASE STYLE'S 98. tabbutton_square.png
  // is 96x57, so TabBarButton's `image-clip: 0 0 98 18` runs two columns off
  // the right edge of its own texture. That pushes the 9-slice's right border
  // out of bounds and leaves the art's real dark right-edge column (x=94-95)
  // inside the STRETCHED middle instead -- so it gets dragged inwards and drawn
  // as a stray dark vertical line across the tab. A stock 20px-wide tab hides
  // it a pixel from the edge; at this tab's ~120-140px it lands in open space.
  // Clipping to the texture's true width pins that edge back where it belongs.
  image-clip: 0 0 96 18
  padding-top: 0
  padding-bottom: 0
  // (!) The width comes from these. UITabBar:addTab sizes a tab to
  // `textSize + paddingLeft + paddingRight` and knows nothing about the icon,
  // so the icon's room has to BE the left padding -- 12 to the glyph, 20 of
  // glyph, 6 of gap. Getting this wrong is what put the label under its own
  // icon; it is not something to patch up with setWidth afterwards.
  padding-left: 38
  padding-right: 16
  font: verdana-11px-antialised
  color: #b9b9b9

  // (!) PADDING DOES NOT MOVE THE TEXT. UIWidget::drawText builds its rect
  // from the widget's FULL screen coords plus text-offset
  // (uiwidgettext.cpp:119) -- padding only feeds the auto-size maths. So
  // padding-left buys the tab its width and text-offset is what actually
  // clears the icon; setting only the former draws the label on top of it.
  text-align: left
  text-offset: 38 0

  // (!) THE SIDE-RAIL ART IS A 40x20 TWO-STATE SHEET: the resting glyph at
  // 0,0 and the lit gold one at 20,0. Without a clip the icon draws at the
  // texture's full 40x20 -- both states squeezed side by side, which is
  // exactly the mangled sliver the first version rendered.
  //
  // Placed by an explicit rect rather than align+offset so it lands at a known
  // x and is properly centred in a 34px tab: (34 - 20) / 2 = 7.
  icon-clip: 0 0 20 20
  icon-rect: 12 7 20 20

  // No icon-color tint. The sheet already carries its own two states, so the
  // selected tab switches to the GOLD half of the art rather than being
  // recoloured -- the same thing the side-button rail does with these files.
  // Both state clips carry the same 96 correction as the resting one above.
  $hover !checked:
    color: #ffffff
    icon-clip: 20 0 20 20
    image-clip: 0 18 96 18

  $checked:
    color: #f0c674
    icon-clip: 20 0 20 20
    image-clip: 0 36 96 18

// ---------------- the window ----------------
//
// Two tabs on one window. Highscores is primary and opens selected; the whole
// achievements view is the second tab, moved into AchTabPanel above without a
// single widget changing. They share a frame because they are one idea from
// the player's side -- what this character has done, and where that puts them
// against everyone else -- and sharing it is also why they share an opcode
// pair rather than burning another from the near-exhausted 0x40-0x4F range.
AchWindow < MainWindow
  // No image-color: the frame keeps the client's own neutral stone so the
  // window sits inside the UI rather than announcing itself, exactly as Bao
  // and the Bazaar do. The palette lives on the panels inside the frame.
  id: achievementsWindow
  !text: tr('Records')
  size: 920 700
  @onEscape: modules.game_achievements.hide()

  RecordsTabBar
    id: mainTabs
    anchors.top: parent.top
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right

  // (!) The tab panels are parented HERE by UITabBar:selectTab, so this must
  // be a real sized panel and not `anchors.fill: parent` on something that
  // also holds the footer -- a filled content area would sit on top of the
  // Close button and swallow its clicks.
  Panel
    id: tabContent
    anchors.top: mainTabs.bottom
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.bottom: closeButton.top
    margin-top: 6
    margin-bottom: 6
  // ---------------- footer ----------------
  // Same chrome as Bao and the Bazaar: Close bottom-right against the frame,
  // status text sharing the row to its left rather than owning a band of its
  // own. Feedback lands here rather than in a popup -- a modal steals focus
  // and hides the thing it is talking about.
  AchButton
    id: closeButton
    !text: tr('Close')
    anchors.right: parent.right
    anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
    width: 64
    @onClick: modules.game_achievements.hide()

  Label
    id: statusLine
    height: 16
    anchors.left: parent.left
    anchors.right: closeButton.left
    anchors.verticalCenter: closeButton.verticalCenter
    margin-right: 12
    font: verdana-11px-monochrome
    color: #9a9a9a
